{"name":"Carbon Dating","hex":"#565b58","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carbon dating","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["radiocarbon dating."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carbon_dating"}],"entries":[{"title":"Radiocarbon dating","blocks":[{"text":"Radiocarbon dating is a method for determining the age of an object containing organic material by using the properties of radiocarbon, a radioactive isotope of carbon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/The_Temple_Scroll_%2811Q20%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/330px-The_Temple_Scroll_%2811Q20%29_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiocarbon_dating","wikidata":"Q173412"},{"title":"Carbon","blocks":[{"text":"Carbon is a chemical element; it has symbol C and atomic number 6. It is nonmetallic and tetravalent—meaning that its atoms are able to form up to four covalent bonds due to its valence shell exhibiting 4 electrons. It belongs to group 14 of the periodic table. Carbon makes up about 0.025 percent of Earth's crust. Three isotopes occur naturally, 12C and 13C being stable, while 14C is a radionuclide, decaying with a half-life of 5,700 years. Carbon is one of the few elements known since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Graphite-and-diamond-with-scale.jpg/330px-Graphite-and-diamond-with-scale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon","wikidata":"Q623"},{"title":"Dating","blocks":[{"text":"Dating is an activity involving spending time with other individuals usually through planned social encounters, with the intention of getting to know each other, often with a romantic or intimate purpose. While the result of dating may at any time lead to friendship, any level of intimate relationship, marriage, or no relation, its significance extends beyond relationship status. Studies in human psychology find that dating can also function as a form of personal growth, as individuals expand their understanding of themselves and others through shared experiences and emotional exchange."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dating","wikidata":"Q654810"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Willard_Libby_in_Lab_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Willard_Libby_in_Lab_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Willard Libby, the inventor of radiocarbon dating","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWillard_Libby_in_Lab_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Hemispheric_14C_graphs_1950s_to_2010.png/500px-Hemispheric_14C_graphs_1950s_to_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Hemispheric_14C_graphs_1950s_to_2010.png/500px-Hemispheric_14C_graphs_1950s_to_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Atmospheric 14C for the northern and southern hemispheres, showing percentage excess above pre-bomb levels. The Partial Test Ban Treaty went into effect on 10 October 1963.[38]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHemispheric_14C_graphs_1950s_to_2010.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/NR_sheep.jpg/500px-NR_sheep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/NR_sheep.jpg/500px-NR_sheep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North Ronaldsay sheep on the beach in North Ronaldsay, Scotland. In the winter, these sheep eat seaweed, which has a higher δ13C content than grass; samples from these sheep have a δ13C value of about −13‰, which is much higher than for sheep that feed on grasses.[45]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANR_sheep.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/1_MV_accelerator_mass_spectrometer.jpg/500px-1_MV_accelerator_mass_spectrometer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/1_MV_accelerator_mass_spectrometer.jpg/500px-1_MV_accelerator_mass_spectrometer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Measuring 14C is now most commonly done with an accelerator mass spectrometer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1_MV_accelerator_mass_spectrometer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Prometheus_tree1.jpg/500px-Prometheus_tree1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Prometheus_tree1.jpg/500px-Prometheus_tree1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The stump of a very old bristlecone pine. Tree rings from these trees (among others) are used in building calibration curves.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrometheus_tree1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Intcal_20_calibration_curve.png/500px-Intcal_20_calibration_curve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Intcal_20_calibration_curve.png/500px-Intcal_20_calibration_curve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Northern hemisphere curve from IntCal20. As of 2020, this is the most recent version of the standard calibration curve. The diagonal l